,"name":"Raffaele Di Mario","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/8f6p3L2SF3bns1auIecRzpCc4Oo.jpg"},{"id":1086865,"name":"Rate Furlan"},{"id":224459,"name":"Livio Galassi","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/uLVKJlZS0QcbYVQcRIXWGuPs0Wr.jpg"},{"id":1855347,"name":"Elena Magoia","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/hdlTH0oDGrHsHavGH4SplNPTcvq.jpg"},{"id":146997,"name":"Piero Vida","profile":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/gwH1Dr6Xvi7NQ1QCwKf4e60uW4R.jpg"}],"crew":[],"videos":[],"watchProviders":[],"episodeGroups":[],"translations":[{"language":"it-IT","title":"Nostalghia","overview":"Un poeta sovietico, Andrej Gorčakov, è in Italia per scrivere la biografia di un compositore russo del XVIII secolo, Andrej Sosnovskij. Insieme a lui è la sua interprete, la bella e irrequieta Eugenia. Durante una tappa a Bagno Vignoni Gorčakov conosce il vecchio Domenico, un uomo ritenuto da tutti matto perché, vari anni prima, è rimasto rinchiuso in casa per 7 anni con la sua famiglia in attesa della fine del mondo. Gorčakov è attratto dall’uomo e va a trovarlo. Durante il lungo dialogo fra i due Domenico affida a Gorčakov la missione di compiere in sua vece un rito salvifico: attraversare con una candela accesa la piscina di acque termali di Bagno Vignoni."},{"language":"en-US","title":"Nostalgia","overview":"Russian poet Andrei Gorchakov journeys through Italy with his interpreter Eugenia to research the life of an 18th-century Russian composer who once lived abroad. Isolated and consumed by an unrelenting longing for his homeland, Andrei becomes drawn to Domenico, a radical mystic obsessed with spiritual redemption. Through austere imagery and extended temporal rhythms, Tarkovsky examines exile, memory, and the profound melancholy of being unable to belong fully to either place or language."},{"language":"ru-RU","overview":"Русский писатель Андрей Горчаков приезжает в Италию в поисках биографических следов крепостного музыканта Павла Сосновского, некогда посетившего эти места. Поиски примет эмиграционных дней жизни музыканта - это и есть то, что связывает Горчакова c переводчицей Юдженией, беспомощно пытающейся понять причину тоски русского друга посредством томика стихов Арсения Тарковского.\r Вскоре Горчаков начинает осознавать, что история музыканта - это отчасти и его собственная история: в Италии он чувствует себя чужим, но и вернуться домой уже не может. Героем овладевает тягостное оцепенение, тоска по родине переходит в болезнь...","tagline":"«Невысказанные чувства никогда не забываются»"}],"images":{"logos":[],"posters":[],"backdrops":[]},"poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/7jlHpPgFgQxt9f5IGTYemGdvIVV.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/z0ZAEC2aZuflzua3HOSygVzE6Jq.jpg","seasons":[],"schema":{}}},"artworkLibrary":{"tmdb":{"schemaVersion":1,"source":"tmdb","id":1394,"type":"movie","originalLanguage":"ru-RU","series":{"poster":{"it":{"status":"available","selected":{"type":"poster","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/7jlHpPgFgQxt9f5IGTYemGdvIVV.jpg","previewUrl":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/7jlHpPgFgQxt9f5IGTYemGdvIVV.jpg","language":"it","width":2000,"height":3000},"candidates":[{"type":"poster","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/7jlHpPgFgQxt9f5IGTYemGdvIVV.jpg","previewUrl":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/7jlHpPgFgQxt9f5IGTYemGdvIVV.jpg","language":"it","width":2000,"height":3000},{"type":"poster","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/iL1znO4eEIaN5k1UOWrPMvueyF6.jpg","previewUrl":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/iL1znO4eEIaN5k1UOWrPMvueyF6.jpg","language":"it","width":1527,"height":2156},{"type":"poster","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/9QjnaEEtYxE4DXygWBuRfFQFyGj.jpg","previewUrl":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/9QjnaEEtYxE4DXygWBuRfFQFyGj.jpg","language":"it","width":1000,"height":1500},{"type":"poster","url":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/xzQ3g6ojWo4pGzEI9J2OsysuTUF.jpg","previewUrl":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/xzQ3g6ojWo4pGz